Recognize F1-F12, Insert, BackTab (Shift-Tab), and modified specials (Shift/Ctrl-arrows, S-Home etc.) as named keys so they can be bound, and normalize forwarded keys to tmux-256color terminfo rather than passing the outer terminal bytes verbatim. Today the tokenizer swallows unrecognized CSI/SS3 as "Unknown" and passes the raw bytes through: this WORKS when the outer terminal encodes a key the same as tmux-256color (true for \E[N~ and SS3 F1-4), but such keys cannot be bound by name, and a divergent outer terminal would mis-send them. Home/End were the only actively-broken case and are fixed (send-Home/End-as-terminfo commit). Lower priority: forwarding is correct for standard terminals; this is bindability + robustness. Audit: infocmp tmux-256color, 2026-08-02. | id:fad4fd9da74b450624c035a68ad3b81b72a78932
